//   u7-r-statutory    cites the 1962 MPC 213.6(1), the provision bar outlines teach. The ALI approved a revised Article 213 in 2022;
//                     its section numbers and mistake-of-age text were not read here, so nothing cites the revised text.
//   u7-r-accomplice   natural and probable consequences as the traditional/common-law reach of accomplice liability.
//   u7-r-intox        MPC 2.08 paraphrase (voluntary intoxication may negate purpose or knowledge, never recklessness).
//   u7-h-fm-abstract  the abstract-versus-as-committed split on "inherently dangerous" felonies (rule stated in the stem).
