            stem: "The jurisdiction recognizes larceny, larceny by trick, embezzlement and false pretenses as separate offenses with their traditional definitions. A man answered an advertisement for a used pickup truck. He told the seller that he had $9,000 in his checking account and handed her a personal check for the $9,000 price. As he knew, the account was empty. Relying on the check, the seller signed the certificate of title over to the man, handed him the keys, and told him that the truck was now his. He drove away, and the bank dishonored the check three days later.",
