            stem: "The jurisdiction defines attempt as at common law. A state statute makes it a crime to possess any controlled substance listed in a schedule; the schedule lists many drugs, but not a certain herbal supplement. A man bought a bag of that supplement from a street vendor. He knew exactly what the bag contained, but he mistakenly believed that the supplement was on the schedule and that possessing it was a crime. Police who saw the sale stopped him and tested the powder, which was the supplement and nothing else. He was charged with attempted possession of a controlled substance.",
