            stem: "By statute, the jurisdiction applies the Model Penal Code's objective test of entrapment. A man had two old convictions for selling prescription painkillers but had held a steady job for six years. An undercover officer posing as a cancer patient befriended him and, for three months, called him almost daily, crying that she was in agony and would kill herself unless he found her pills, and offering him ten times the street price. He finally bought pills from a dealer and sold them to her. He was charged with selling a controlled substance and raised entrapment.",
